   254	Plant materials were cleaned and the inedible portions were
   255	removed. The edible parts were rinsed thoroughly with tap
   256	water and then with distilled water. The washed plant
   257	materials were dried with clean cloth, were cut into very small
   258	pieces, frozen in liquid nitrogen, freeze-dried and kept at -20 0
   259	C until analysis [11].
   260	One gm of freeze-dried tubers were soaked in 10 ml water.
   261	Then 1 ml 0.1 M and 10 ml phosphate buffer (1M, pH 5.5)
